**Definition 6.1 (seven-family memory body).** Serialize precisely UAS
Definition 3.3's independently existing selection, not a complete trace or
completed-cycle list. The body is an exact seven-field tuple. Family $f$
is the five-field tuple

$$
[U(f),\mathcal L(\mathrm{cells}_f),\mathcal L(\mathrm{slots}_f),
       \mathcal L(\mathrm{relations}_f),\mathcal L(\mathrm{frontier}_f)].
$$

Use the following fixed meanings and order:

| $f$ | Actual selected material |
| --- | --- |
| 0 | Acquired seed 26/designated initial interval; actual seed/boot delivery 28/29 backing and $H_0,\xi$ binding. |
| 1 | Constructed finite version/bootstrap slots, stage/cursor fields, captured field zero and constructed initial 69 prefix, with its actual 68 bindings. Later staging is excluded from this prefix. |
| 2 | Chronological 13 header/length/payload backing and actual 17 descriptors/origins, including partial current records and unwritten allocated payload material. |
| 3 | Actual 70 chain after its one sentinel and its constructed 68 ingress descriptors, including partial current material. |
| 4 | Actual version/PC/call site/role permutation, relevant marked ingress/length heads, live base/length/counters 1–12 during 13 ingress or 66/67 during 70 ingress, and the uniquely occupied input latch only before its matching WR. |
| 5 | Actual constructed cover/package/publication backing 71, acquired receiver backing/bindings 73 and actual invocation/read/mailbox relations, including partial unavailable records. |
| 6 | Actual meter cells/marks and current token/stage slots determining the selected resources' rights. |

A cell entry is `[U(port),U(creationPosition),eightTracks]`. A slot entry
is `[U(slotCatalogIndex),value]`, with value 0 for absent, 10 for present 0,
11 for present 1. A relation entry is `[U(kind),endpoints,rawFields]`.
Here a cell reference is `[0,U(port),U(position)]`, a finite-slot reference
`[1,U(slotIndex)]`, and a span `[U(port),U(base),U(constructedLength)]`.
Optional is exactly 0 or `1 Frame(value)`. Reference identities are checked
against the reconstructed actual history. An endpoint outside the selected
spans, such as intermediate mailbox 72 or a remote origin, carries identity
only; it does not import that endpoint's payload or grant a read. The six
fixed schemas are:

| kind | endpoints, exact arity | rawFields, exact arity |
| --- | --- | --- |
| 0 descriptor | `[descriptorSpan,backingSpan]` | `[grammarBit,rawSymbolTriples,optionalParsedFields,optionalStatusReference]`; grammar 0 is CAP's ten fields, grammar 1 RCA's six grouped fields. Parsed fields are absent on an incomplete descriptor. |
| 1 origin-copy | `[sourceSpan,destinationSpan]` | `[completeOrigin,U(copiedExtent),optionalCompletionReference]`. |
| 2 seal | `[sealedSpan]` | `[sealCellReference,eightSealTracks,availabilityValue]`. |
| 3 availability | `[sourceSlotReference,destinationSlotReference]` | `[sourceValue,destinationValue]`, each in the slot-value code. |
| 4 initial binding | `[seedSpan,bootSpan,optionalCaptureSpan]` | `[xi,U(H0),completeDeliveryReference,optionalCodeChain]`. |
| 5 object span | `[constructedSpan]` | `[U(objectKind),U(callPathIndex),optionalDeclaredLength,availabilityValue,optionalCompleteOrigin]`. |

DescriptorSpan and backingSpan contain their actually constructed prefix,
not a predicted future extent. RawSymbolTriples includes delimiters already
constructed; no complete parsed tuple is substituted for partial bytes.
Object kinds are seed, initial field, input header, input length, input
payload, cover, package, sender, mailbox, receiver, completion, in that order.
All parsed/extent annotations are redundant values computed from the
selected span/frontier or its actual construction relation; none is an
extra historical input. No relation is emitted before its construction;
partial object spans retain raw prefixes and unavailable status. Missing
optional status/completion/capture is explicit, not a fictitious reference.

A frontier entry is `[U(role),value]` in the static order version, PC,
phase, role permutation, ingress head, length head, base, remaining length,
counter, pending. Values are the actual finite words or marked creation
positions; pending is 0 outside its interval, else `1 Frame([site,bit])`.
These are descriptions of selected existing fields, not newly installed
frontier registers. A not-applicable entry is the empty list. Preserve a
selected raw scratch word as its cell records as well as its marked role;
do not silently replace a partially constructed numeral by an integer.

Order structures as the table, cells by port/creation position, slots by
catalog index, relations by kind/endpoints/raw-fields lexicographic order,
frontier by its listed role. Suppress duplicate physical entries within a
family; references in different families still name the same physical
identity. Alias equality is exact reference equality. Boundaries/markers
needed to delimit each selected backing span are included with that span.
An empty family component has the literal empty-list encoding.

